W44-112 Layer-1.5 quant_field discriminator (INTERNAL vs PRODUCTION)
====================================================================

Base commit:  9f3c4062 (W44-111 — butteraugli metric divergence RULED OUT)
Date:         2026-05-20
Hostname:     lilith
Builder:      cargo, rustc release profile (CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target)
Features:     __internal_recon_hook butteraugli-loop
Reproducer:   cargo run --release --quiet -p jxl-encoder \
                --example w44_112_qf_discriminator \
                --features '__internal_recon_hook butteraugli-loop' \
                --manifest-path jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml \
                > benchmarks/w44_112_qf_discriminator_2026-05-20.tsv

Cells (W44-111 mirror set):
  - terminal e8 d=4.0      (gb82-sc, 1646×1062)
  - terminal e8 d=2.0      (gb82-sc, 1646×1062)
  - 1025469 e8 d=2.0       (CID22-512, 512×512)
  - 1025469 e8 d=4.0       (CID22-512, 512×512)

Per-block CSV dumps (one file per cell, optional):
  /tmp/w44_112/perblock_{image}_{d}_e{eff}.csv
  Columns: bx,by,raw_strategy,is_first,internal_qf,production_qf,diff

Method
------

For each cell:
  1. Enable BOTH `recon_hook` (captures final-iter `quant_field_u8` from buttloop)
     AND `production_qf` hook (captures `quant_field_u8` from
     `transform_and_quantize_with_source` after AdjustQuantBlockAC has been
     applied to all parallel groups).
  2. Encode via LossyConfig::new(d).with_effort(8) (production default pipeline,
     including the W44-105 screenshot qac-scale on screenshot cells at d>=2).
  3. Diff per-block: int_qf vs prod_qf u8.
  4. Also capture `DistanceParams.{global_scale, scale, inv_scale}` from BOTH
     sides — InternalRecon snapshots the buttloop's final-iter `current_params`,
     ProductionQf snapshots the params handed to production transform.

Discriminator interpretation
----------------------------

  - If int_qf == prod_qf per-block AND params match → candidates 1 (SetQuantField
    inv_scale drift) and 2 (parallel-vs-sequential AdjustQuantBlockAC) RULED OUT.
    Drill candidate 3 (recon vs decoder pixel pipeline) in W44-113.
  - If int_qf != prod_qf → candidate 1 or 2 in play; drill further by checking
    whether the divergence concentrates in specific strategies / specific
    `quant_adjustments` patterns.

