Verdict
-------

**Candidates 1 and 2 RULED OUT.** Zero per-block divergence across 62,988 blocks
(4 cells × all blocks). DistanceParams byte-identical INT vs PROD for every cell.

The buttloop's final-iter quantized output IS the same as production's quantized
output. The R/G residual ~0.05 max-abs in linear RGB documented in
quality_drift_investigation_2026-05-15 (chunk-3 followup) MUST come from
candidate 3: a divergence in the pixel pipeline AFTER quantization, between
`reconstruct_xyb` (buttloop side) and the decoder's render path (jxl-rs / djxl
/ jxl-oxide side).

Note: production_qf is captured in `transform_and_quantize_with_source` which is
NOT called when bitstream-emit goes through alternative paths (e.g. precomputed
fast-path `EncoderPrecomputed::compute_with_budget`). For the API-level
default-effort-8 encode tested here the wrapper IS the right capture site.

W44-113 plan
------------

Attack candidate 3:

  a) Compare `dequant_bias` / `AdjustQuantBias` application in `reconstruct_xyb`
     vs decoder pipeline. CLAUDE.md notes both use `kDefaultQuantBias` (Resolved
     Bugs section / AC strategy investigation note) but the application *order*
     vs CfL pass / LLF subtraction may differ. Existing memo `drift_block_map.rs`
     (chunk-3 diagnostic, 2026-05-15) clustered B-channel residual by
     `cfl_ytob != 0` (3× rate). With CfL pass-2 now BEFORE the buttloop the
     ytob input is at parity going in; if the application step still diverges
     the residual is in the dequant_bias step.

  b) Per-block diff map extended to R/G channels (mirroring chunk-2's B-channel
     diagnostic). Where do R/G residuals concentrate? If they correlate with
     specific AC strategies (e.g. AFV, DCT4X4, DCT2X2 — the small-block variants
     the chunk-2 table showed 20-40% divergent), the bug is in the buttloop's
     `transform_and_quantize_into → reconstruct_xyb` chain's strategy-specific
     IDCT or LLF handling vs the decoder's corresponding paths.

  c) (escape hatch) Replace buttloop's internal recon with a real encode→decode
     roundtrip on the FINAL iter — slower but eliminates the divergence in one
     step. Useful as a regression backstop if (a)+(b) take more than one chunk.

Production code change in W44-112: ZERO. Only investigation infra:

  - `jxl-encoder/src/vardct/butteraugli_loop.rs` — `InternalRecon` struct gains
    3 fields (`final_{global_scale,scale,inv_scale}`); new `ProductionQf` struct
    + `set/take_production_qf` API in the `recon_hook` module. All gated on
    `feature = "__internal_recon_hook"` (zero cost at production builds).
  - `jxl-encoder/src/vardct/transform.rs` — `transform_and_quantize_with_source`
    grows a feature-gated capture point at its tail (1 atomic load + 1 vec
    clone when enabled; cheap atomic-load early-exit when disabled).
  - `jxl-encoder/examples/w44_112_qf_discriminator.rs` — new example.
  - `jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml` — registered new example.

No hash-lock invalidation, no test changes.
